<section class="alt" id="cli">
  <div class="container two-col">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Command line</p>
      <h2>Your hotkeys, your rules.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        BrightSync does not ship a hotkey daemon. Bind the CLI in AutoHotkey, PowerToys, your desktop's shortcut
        settings or a script, and it talks to the running tray app.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">On Windows the command is <code>BrightSync.exe</code>; on Linux it is <code>brightsync</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="c"># one-shot, works even when the tray app is not running</span>
brightsync brightness set 55
brightsync brightness up 10
brightsync brightness down 10

<span class="c"># talk to the running tray app</span>
brightsync status --json
brightsync auto on
brightsync eye-protection on --hours 3
brightsync boost on --hours 2
brightsync monitors refresh</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>
